<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" version="1.1" creator="trip-planner">
  <metadata>
    <name>AZ Grand Tour: Fools Loop + Queen&apos;s Ransom + AZT + Mt Lemmon + Madrean Rugged Ramble (by section)</name>
    <desc>Stitched bikepacking route: Fool&apos;s Loop (bikepacking.com) -&gt; link 1b via the Arizona Canal -&gt; Queen&apos;s Ransom (bikepacking.com) -&gt; road to Kearny and back -&gt; Arizona Trail (AZTR AZT300_SBXL_2026_v3) to Oracle -&gt; Mt Lemmon Control Road (bikepacking.com Redington-Lemmon Loop) -&gt; Catalina Highway down from Summerhaven -&gt; Bug Spring Trail -&gt; AZT (Molino, Bellota) -&gt; Madrean Rugged Ramble through Saguaro NP and on the AZT to Kentucky Camp -&gt; AZT to the SR-82 underpass with the AZTR Legacy Patagonia detour -&gt; AZT / Madrean Rugged Ramble to Parker Canyon Lake -&gt; Madrean Rugged Ramble via Lochiel and Patagonia to Tucson. 1322 km, ~21334 m climbing. Source trackpoints are copied verbatim; connectors routed on OpenStreetMap.</desc>
  </metadata>
